# === vLLM Trust Remote Code (v19.1.16+) ===
# VLLM_TRUST_FLAG — computed by scarlix-mode from models.yaml vllm.trust_remote_code.
#   true|1|yes → --trust-remote-code passed to vLLM startup command
#   (empty)    → no flag (vLLM uses its default: no trust)
# This enables running models with custom Python code (e.g. some Qwen/DeepSeek
# architectures). ONLY set trust_remote_code: true for models from trusted HF
# sources — untrusted code runs with the vLLM container's permissions.
# This variable is auto-generated by scarlix-mode into /opt/scarlix/.env.
# Do NOT set it manually unless you understand the security implications.
# VLLM_TRUST_FLAG=--trust-remote-code  # uncomment ONLY for trusted custom-code models
